{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789862343,"nonce":"1YD0saZv8jvQfs0SUMHiTdKGoMU=","title":"Task: Remove bleve entirely (needs a pristine-boundary call)","message":"Follow-up from 3500366, which removed every *use* of bleve: no index is created, nothing in cache/ touches it, and text search is a substring match over excerpts.\n\nThe dependency itself survives. repository/index_bleve.go implements the pristine RepoIndex interface with it, and //AGENTS.md puts repository/ off limits, so deleting it is a boundary decision before it is a code change.\n\nWhat it buys: ~20 modules out of the graph (blevesearch/* plus zapx v11-v17), a smaller binary, and one less thing for go.mod audits and govulncheck to walk.\n\nWhat it costs: repository/index_bleve.go deleted, the RepoIndex/Index interfaces removed from repository/repo.go, GetIndex dropped from the mock and test repos. That is a real divergence from upstream in one of the seven pristine packages, so future cherry-picks touching repository/ get harder. It is also a one-way door in practice: re-adding a full-text index later would mean designing it ourselves rather than inheriting it.\n\nRelated: 23eb77f (pristine boundary), 14900ef (graduation criteria). Decide together with the other two deferred pristine edits — the keyring service name and the git-bug.* config namespace (see doc/design/fork-foundations.md, D5).","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789862343,"nonce":"fTCL1T4bs0nvrM29jPtp/3h/jq0=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789862343,"nonce":"bbV3/+Ts9+imijE50F/OdgsriLw=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}